    "https://union.ku.edu/jobs": {
      "title": "Human Resources",
      "description": "KU Memorial Unions Human Resources | KU Memorial Unions Skip to main content The University of Kansas MENU link to menu page THE UNIVERSITY of KANSAS Student Affairs KU Memorial Unions myKU Email Canvas Enroll & Pay Jayhawk GPS Close Search this unit Start search Submit Search Main navigation Home About Select to follow link Our Locations Select to follow link Kansas Union Burge Union DeBruce Center Danforth Chapel About The KU Memorial Union Directors Student Programs & Involvement Strategic Plan 2025 Annual Review Book with us Select to follow link Book with us Event Policies & Procedures Parking Browse Events Elevate your Game Day KU Bookstore KU Dining KU History Select to follow link Exhibits & Tours Stories Work With Us Info for Prospective Students Current Students Alumni Degree Programs myKU Email Canvas Enroll & Pay Jayhawk GPS THE UNIVERSITY of KANSAS University of Kansas logo Student Affairs KU Memorial Unions Menu link to menu page Search this unit Start search Submit Search Home Human Resources Join us and make a difference in a thriving campus community!  Our 1000+ team members are dedicated to our values: Community, Dignity, Empowerment, Excellence, Innovation, and Safety. Job Opportunities Student Part-Time Join the largest student employer on the KU Campus, where we prioritize your academics and offer the best flexible scheduling. Experience the opportunity to learn, work, and serve while being part of our dynamic team. All student positions are eligible for Federal Work Study opportunities. Open Positions Part-Time Career We offer part-time positions at KU Memorial Union that provide a unique opportunity to learn, work, and serve while creating unforgettable moments for our valued KU students. Open Positions Full-Time Career We offer full-time positions at KU Memorial Union that provide a unique opportunity to learn, work, and serve while creating unforgettable moments for our valued KU students. Open Positions Perks and Benefits - Health Insurance - Dental Insurance - Vision Insurance - Paid Time Off, Holiday Pay, and Paid Parental Leave - Matching 403(b) Retirement Plan Health Savings Account (HSA) - Flexible Spending Accounts (Section 125 Pre-Tax Savings Plan) - Basic Life and AD&D - Long-Term Disability Insurance - Mental Health Support 24/7/365 plus grief counseling and estate planning support - Supplemental insurance offerings such as Accident, Hospital Indemnity, Critical Care, Cancer Protection and Critical Illness, Short-Term Disability, and more. - Campus Discounts at the KU Bookstore, KU Dining, Ambler Recreation Center, and more! Student Perks 20 Available Hours Per Week $11-15 Starting Pay Range Matthew Garrett \"If I had to describe my job in three words, it would be \"all about people\". I chose these three words because that's what my favorite thing about KU Dining is; the people! Not only am I grateful to have so many coworkers who I can call my friends, but I also have the privilege to be one of the first faces people see on campus when they come to tour. I can be the person that makes someone's day on campus be just a little bit better.\" Career Statistics 7.5% Retirement Contribution 5 years of average tenure 85 Promotions awarded in 2024 Union Human Resources unionhr@ku.edu Phone: 785-864-2450 Fax: 785-864-5227 Kansas Union\n \n                                                    , \n570 1301 Jayhawk Blvd Lawrence\n, \nKansas\n \n66045 Frequently Asked Questions How is the Memorial Union related to the University of Kansas? Click to expand The Memorial Union is a non-profit affiliate of the University of Kansas. As KU's community center and the heart of campus, we are dedicated to serving the University and its community. Our mission is to provide inviting spaces, inspiring programs, and high-quality facilities, services, and conveniences for the entire University community. What kind of jobs are available? Click to expand At the Memorial Union, we offer a wide range of job opportunities that cover every aspect of our operations. Here's a glimpse into the diverse roles you can find within our organization: 1. Dining: We have over 18 dining locations, each offering unique culinary experiences. From chefs and servers to baristas and kitchen staff, there are numerous opportunities to contribute to our vibrant dining scene.  So many leadership opportunities for advancement with part time and full time schedules. ‍ 2. Administrative and Leadership: Our administrative and leadership roles play a crucial role in keeping our operations running smoothly. These positions encompass various departments, ensuring effective coordination and strategic decision-making. ‍ 3. Bookstore: Our bustling bookstore operation is where retail meets academia. We offer positions related to retail sales, textbook merchandise, customer service, and more, providing a dynamic environment for those passionate about the intersection of education and commerce. ‍ 4. Catering and Event Services: Our catering and event services team is responsible for orchestrating thousands of events each year. Whether it's coordinating logistics, providing exceptional service, or creating memorable experiences, this department offers exciting opportunities for individuals with a flair for hospitality. ‍ 5. Building Services: Our buildings are more than just structures; they're inviting spaces that foster a positive environment. Our building services positions focus on maintaining the aesthetic appeal and functionality of our facilities, ensuring they are up-to-date and welcoming to all. In addition to this diverse range of positions, we offer both full-time and part-time jobs tailored to suit the needs of students and non-students alike. Whether you're seeking a career-oriented role or a flexible job that accommodates your studies or other commitments, we have opportunities that align with your goals. Parking and Transportation Click to expand All of our locations on campus are bus route accessible. Students have the option to purchase parking passes through parking.ku.edu. What is E-Verify and how is it used during the hiring process? Click to expand E-Verify confirms employment authorization of all newly hired employees and most existing employees through an electronic database maintained by the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security. For new hires, the E-Verify process is completed in conjunction with the Form I-9 Employment Eligibility Verification on or before the first day of work. E-Verify is not used as a tool to pre-screen candidates. For up-to-date information on E-Verify, go to www.uscis.gov and click on 'E-Verify' located near the bottom of the page. What portion of health insurance does the company pay? Click to expand At the Memorial Union, we prioritize the well-being of our employees and understand the importance of affordable healthcare. Each year, during open enrollment, we evaluate the new insurance rates to ensure that our employees receive the best possible coverage. Despite the rising costs, we are committed to keeping this benefit affordable for our team. In fact, we contribute over 50% towards each insurance option. How often do employees receive raises? Click to expand At the Memorial Union, we believe in recognizing and rewarding our employees' hard work and dedication. With each budget cycle, measured from July to June, we prioritize our employees' rate of pay. You can expect consistent cost-of-living adjustments (COLA) announced with the start of each budget year. But we don't stop there! We also provide performance incentives in the form of one-time payments to recognize exceptional achievements. Additionally, we foster a culture of internal promotions, offering increased responsibility and correlated pay as employees progress in their careers with us. What does 7.5% retirement contribution mean? Click to expand We value the long-term financial security of our employees. After one year of employment, all full-time and part-time non-student employees are eligible to receive a 7.5% contribution to their established retirement plan. To qualify for this employer contribution, employees simply need to contribute 5% of their pre-tax rate. It's our way of investing in your future and ensuring a stable retirement. What is the employee assistance program? Click to expand Your well-being matters to us, both inside and outside of work. That's why we offer an Employee Assistance Program (EAP) to all our employees. This comprehensive program provides access to free counseling sessions, emergency services advice, and legal assistance for both you and your dependents. This confidential service is available 24/7, ensuring that you have the support you need, whenever you need it. When am I eligible for benefits? Click to expand As a full-time employee, you become eligible for benefits after completing two full months of employment. This includes enrolling in our comprehensive health insurance and participating in our retirement plan. The company's contribution towards your retirement begins after one year of employment, setting you on the path towards long-term financial stability. Join our team at the Memorial Union, where we not only prioritize your professional growth but also your overall well-being. We're committed to providing competitive benefits that enhance your life and empower you to thrive. What is E-Verify and how is it used during the hiring process? Click to expand E-Verify confirms employment authorization of all newly hired employees and most existing employees through an electronic database maintained by the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security. For new hires, the E-Verify process is completed in conjunction with the Form I-9 Employment Eligibility Verification on or before the first day of work. E-Verify is not used as a tool to pre-screen candidates. For up-to-date information on E-Verify, go to www.uscis.gov and click on 'E-Verify' located near the bottom of the page. Follow us on social! Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Kansas Union 1301 Jayhawk Blvd. Lawrence, KS 66045 Bus Routes: 10 11 29 30 34 36 38 41 42 43 44 union@ku.edu 785-864-4651 facebook instagram twitter linkedin Join the Team Union Building Hours KU Dining Services KU Bookstore Union Programs Visit KU KU Admissions KU Endowment KU News KU Events KU Careers KU Alumni Nondiscrimination statement Accessibility | Website support | CMS login © 2026 The University of Kansas The University of Kansas prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, status as a veteran, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in the university's programs and activities. Retaliation is also prohibited by university policy. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the nondiscrimination policies and procedures and is the Title IX Coordinator for all KU and KUMC campuses: Associate Vice Chancellor for the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX, civilrights@ku.edu , Room 1082, Dole Human Development Center, 1000 Sunnyside Avenue, Lawrence, KS 66045, 785-864-6414 , 711 TTY. Reports can be submitted by contacting the Title IX Coordinator as provided herein or using the Title IX online report form and complaints can be submitted with the Title IX Coordinator or using the Title IX online complaint form . The University of Kansas is a public institution governed by the Kansas Board of Regents."
    },
    "https://kuendowment.org/home/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers - KU Endowment Skip to content Facebook Twitter Linkedin Youtube Instagram [email protected] 800-444-4201 What’s New Latest Stories All News Donor Impact Faculty & Student Support Crimson & Blue Magazine Spring 2026 Fall 2025 All Issues KU Giving Archive Get Involved Giving Societies Chancellors Club Deans Club Jayhawk Faithful Watkins Society KU Alumni Presidents Club Groups & Partners One Day One KU Advancement Board Class Legacy Walk Companies & Foundations Events David Booth \"Stay Calm\" Book Launch Ways to Give How to Give Online Mail, Phone, Wire Matching Gifts Endowed Funds Giving Options Areas of Support LaunchKU Memorials Planned Giving Planned Gifts Gifts of Securities Gifts of Real Estate Resources & Info Who We Are Overview Mission, Vision, Values & Goals Donor Commitment Leadership Board of Trustees Quick Links KU Faculty & Staff Third Party Fundraising Toolkit Student Loans Connect Contact Us Staff Directory Careers Campaign Search... Give Give Careers As an employee at KU Endowment, you’ll witness firsthand the power of Jayhawk generosity. Overview Open Positions Benefits The people who support KU Endowment’s mission are a talented, fun group who have a passion for helping the University of Kansas achieve its aspirations. KU Endowment is a nonprofit organization, separate from the university and the state of Kansas. We are the official foundation for raising and managing private funds on behalf of KU. Many university foundations help cover their operating costs by charging fees on gifts, but we allocate 100% of the principal of every gift for the purpose designated by the donor. We employ about 160 people in areas such as development (fundraising), accounting, information systems, administrative support and communications. We seek people who share our core values and a commitment to our mission to “partner with donors in providing philanthropic support to build a greater University of Kansas.” It is the policy and commitment of The Kansas University Endowment Association to prohibit discrimination in employment practices, organizational activities and provision of services on the basis of race, national origin, color, creed, religion, sex, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other consideration made unlawful by applicable law. View Open Positions KU Endowment participates in E-Verify . Immigrants and Employee Right to Work Information. Make A Gift Support your passion by making a gift that impacts the lives of students, faculty, patients, and researchers for generations to come. On their behalf, we thank you for your generosity. Give Now P.O. Box 928 Lawrence, KS 66044-0928 785-832-7400 or 800-444-4201 Ways to Give Online Giving Other Options Planned Giving LaunchKU Quick Links Reports & Financials Investment Policies Student Loans KU Faculty & Staff More Info Give Contact Us Careers Update Contact Info Facebook Twitter Linkedin Youtube Instagram Copyright © 2026 Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions"
    },
    "https://kualumni.org/career-opportunities/": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Career Opportunities - KU Alumni Skip to content MY PROFILE Search … GIVE Give Give Give to KU Alumni Presidents Club Jayhawk License Plates Programs & Networks Programs & Networks Supporting KU Volunteer Awards Jayhawks for Higher Ed NextGen Jayhawks Jayhawks Give Back Career Jayhawk Career Network KU Mentoring+ Mocktails & Mingle Webinars The Water Cooler Alumni Job Board Hire Jayhawks Find Your Network Networks & Groups Watch Parties Endacott Society Student Alumni Network Student Alumni Ambassadors More Programs Flying Jayhawks Travel Flying Jayhawk Trips Jayhawk Book Club Jayhawk Pet of the Month TGIT Stories & Events Stories & Events Stories Events Calendar Watch Parties Rock Chalk Forever Homecoming Resources & Info Resources & Info About Us Mission & Vision Staff Directory Career Opportunities Board of Directors Board Roster Nominate a Board Member Resources Business Directory Volunteer Reunions KU Alumni App KU Alumni Shop Scholarships Advertisers & Partners​ Corporate Partners Advertising Opportunities Sponsorship Opportunities Demographics & Profiles Pay Invoice My Profile View Profile Update Information Registration Change Password Submit Class Notes Email Subscriptions Profile Help Jayhawk Welcome Center Jayhawk Welcome Center About the Jayhawk Welcome Center Jayhawk Welcome Center Venues Connect Connect Contact Us Career Opportunities Admissions Reps Search … Career Opportunities Full Time Opportunities Event Services Coordinator or Assistant Director of Event Services Posted 07/10/26 – Review of applications begins 08/11/26 and continues until position is filled. See Application Procedure below for details. There are no open positions at this time. Student Opportunities KU Alumni occasionally offers part-time employment opportunities, internships and graduate assistantships for undergraduate and graduate students. Qualifications differ for each position, and availability varies. Check back regularly for new opportunities. There are no open positions at this time. Application Procedure - Full Time To apply, email a letter of interest with résumé and names and contact information for three professional references to dparman@kualumni.org (Microsoft Word or Adobe PDF formats only). Alternatively, the requested information can be sent to KU Alumni, Attn. Human Resources, 1266 Oread Ave., Lawrence, KS 66045. Review of applications will begin upon receipt and continue until the position is filled. Due to the sensitive nature of the position, a background check is required. Employment is contingent upon background and reference checks that KU Alumni finds to be acceptable. If you are called for an interview, you will also be asked to complete our job application and bring it with you to the interview. Application Procedure - Student To apply, send a letter of interest and résumé, along with the names and contact information for three professional references to dparman@kualumni.org . Alternatively, the requested information can be mailed or brought to KU Alumni, Attn. Human Resources, 1266 Oread Ave., Lawrence, KS 66045. If you are called for an interview, you will also be asked to complete our job application and bring it with you to the interview. Our Values Appreciate The Unique We empower our community to authentically shine. We believe that differences are strengths, all humanity has value and all Jayhawks belong. Cultivate The Core We co-construct shared experiences and memories extending from KU’s campus to our global community, connected by what it means to be a Jayhawk. Fuel The Future We bravely reimagine the future together and boldly innovate to continue raising the standard for Jayhawk Excellence. Mission KU Alumni is a trusted, strategic partner in advancing the mission of the University of Kansas by uniting a global network of Jayhawks and increasing the value of KU degrees. Through the support of donors and friends, KU Alumni positively impacts the University of Kansas in five ways: We Advocate, Communicate, Recruit, Serve, and Unite Jayhawks . Mission/Commitment KU Alumni is a trusted, strategic partner in advancing the mission of the University of Kansas by uniting a global network of Jayhawks and increasing the value of KU degrees. Through the support of donors and friends, KU Alumni positively impacts the University of Kansas in five ways: We Advocate, Communicate, Recruit, Serve, and Unite Jayhawks . Equal Opportunity Employer As an equal opportunity employer, it is the policy and commitment of KU Alumni to prohibit discrimination in employment practices, organizational activities and provision of services on the basis of race, ethnicity, ancestry, national origin, religion, age, gender, marital or domestic partner status, sexual orientation, gender identity, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. Other Opportunities Looking for other opportunities to advance your career? Check out the Jayhawk Career Network where you can network with KU alumni, join our LinkedIn group and find other resources to help with your job search. We build lifelong relationships that strengthen the University of Kansas and the legacy of excellence embodied by its students, alumni, faculty, staff and friends. Jayhawk Welcome Center at Adams Alumni Center 1266 Oread Ave., Lawrence, KS 66045 kualumni@kualumni.org  | 800.584.2957 Most Visited Jayhawk Career Network Student Alumni Network Watch Parties Events Calendar Stories Jayhawk Welcome Center Quicklinks About Us Staff Directory Crimson & Blue magazine Corporate Partners Employment Opportunities Privacy & Terms Campus Partners The University of Kansas KU Endowment Kansas Athletics KU Admissions KU Bookstore Jayhawk Community Partners Facebook Youtube Instagram Linkedin Copyright © 2026 Most Visited Jayhawk Career Network Student Alumni Network Watch Parties Events Calendar Stories Jayhawk Welcome Center Quicklinks About Us Staff Directory Crimson & Blue magazine Corporate Partners Employment Opportunities Privacy & Terms Campus Partners The University of Kansas KU Endowment Kansas Athletics KU Admissions KU Bookstore Jayhawk Community Partners Facebook Youtube Instagram Linkedin Copyright © 2026 Welcome to KU Alumni Your gift to KU Alumni is the single most powerful way to make all of KU stronger, including the value of your own degree. Through your support, KU Alumni: Enhances student recruitment & programming Increases the value of your KU degree Preserves KU’s distinctive, nationally known traditions Provides an avenue for advocates for KU and its impact Grows and connects a larger network of Jayhawks Learn More Learn More Make a Gift Make a Gift Support KU Alumni Jayhawk Career Network Stories Networks & Groups Insert/edit link Close Enter the destination URL URL Link Text Open link in a new tab Or link to existing content Search No search term specified. Showing recent items. Search or use up and down arrow keys to select an item. Cancel"
