    "https://www.kumc.edu/human-resources/careers.html": {
      "title": "Human Resources",
      "description": "Careers Skip to main content. kumc.edu School of Health Professions School of Medicine School of Nursing University of Kansas The University of Kansas Health System The University of Kansas Cancer Center Search within this section Search all sites Human Resources Careers The University of Kansas Health System KU-Wichita Medical Practice Association KU School of Pharmacy University of Kansas Benefits New Employees About Our Campuses Info for School of Health Professions School of Medicine School of Nursing Current Students Blackboard Webmail myKUMC Prospective Students Prospective Employees Alumni Faculty & Staff Residents & Fellows Patients Donors Researchers Visitors Human Resources Our Campuses Make a Gift Info for Human Resources Careers Careers The University of Kansas Health System KU-Wichita Medical Practice Association KU School of Pharmacy University of Kansas Benefits Benefits Insurance Programs Time Off & Leave Retirement Employee Assistance Program Other Benefits Ending Employment at KU Medical Center New Employees About About Meet the HR Staff Employee Spotlights Forms Campus Policies Diversity and Nondiscrimination Training Materials We're looking for employees to serve our community through excellence in education, research, patient care and community engagement. View Career Opportunities Benefits Join KU Medical Center As you consider joining the KU Medical Center team, we invite you to learn a bit more about the benefits we offer and some of the features that set us apart. Accommodations KU Medical Center encourages qualified individuals with disabilities to apply. To request accommodations to complete an online job application, please contact Human Resources at 913-588-5080 or hr-university@kumc.edu . Clinical Partner Requirements KU Medical Center works closely with its clinical partners, including The University of Kansas Health System.  Any KU Medical Center employee that works in a physical location managed by or shared with The University of Kansas Health System or other clinical partner may be subject to the partner's workplace safety policies, including vaccine requirements. Additional Career Opportunities The University of Kansas Medical Center is an educational and research institution. We encourage you to explore additional career opportunities with our clinical and educational partners. The University of Kansas Health System Our clinical partner provides patient care and operates the hospital located on our shared campus. KU-Wichita Medical Practice Association KU School of Medicine-Wichita Medical Practice Association employs individuals who provide care and assist with the operations of outpatient clinics. KU School of Pharmacy With campuses in Wichita and Lawrence, the School of Pharmacy has a separate hiring system. University of Kansas Explore a variety of open positions at the flagship campus of the University of Kansas. Policies Clery Annual Security Report Kansas Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) Nondiscrimination, Equal Opportunity, and Affirmative Action Policy Pay Transparency Notice Title IX Human Resources Human Resources-KC 3901 Rainbow Blvd 1044 Delp Kansas City, KS 66160 913-588-5080 KU Medical Center-Wichita Human Resources 1010 N. Kansas Wichita, KS 67214 316-293-2615 Make a Gift 3901 Rainbow Boulevard, Kansas City, KS 66160 | 913-588-5000 About Calendar News Careers Facebook opens in new tab Twitter opens in new tab YouTube opens in new tab Instagram opens in new tab LinkedIn opens in new tab © 2026 The University of Kansas prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, status as a veteran, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in the university’s programs and activities. Retaliation is also prohibited by university policy. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the nondiscrimination policies and procedures and is the Title IX Coordinator for all KU and KUMC campuses: Associate Vice Chancellor for the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX, civilrights@ku.edu , Room 1082, Dole Human Development Center, 1000 Sunnyside Avenue, Lawrence, KS 66045, 785-864-6414, 711 TTY. Reports can be submitted by contacting the Title IX Coordinator as provided herein or using the Title IX online report form and complaints can be submitted with the Title IX Coordinator or using the Title IX online complaint form . Free Expression Statement | Privacy Statement | Notice of Privacy Practices | Consumer Information We use cookies to analyze our traffic & provide social media features. Visit the KU Medical Center Privacy Statement for more information. By closing this window & browsing this site, you agree to our use of cookies."
    },
    "https://career.ku.edu/ptjobs": {
      "title": "Part-Time Student Jobs",
      "description": "Part-Time Jobs | University Career Center Skip to main content The University of Kansas MENU link to menu page THE UNIVERSITY of KANSAS Academic Success University Career Center myKU Email Canvas Enroll & Pay Jayhawk GPS Close Search this unit Start search Submit Search Main navigation Home About Select to follow link About Us Contact Us People KU Employment Data Career Advising Career Resources Student Pathways Events Select to follow link Career Partners Summer Institute 2026 Select to follow link 2026 Career Partners Summer Institute Faculty Info for Graduate Students Faculty Employers Alumni myKU Email Canvas Enroll & Pay Jayhawk GPS THE UNIVERSITY of KANSAS University of Kansas logo Academic Success University Career Center Menu link to menu page Search this unit Start search Submit Search Home Students Jobs & Internships Part-Time Student Jobs Both on-campus and off-campus student jobs are available to KU students. Our goal is to assist University of Kansas students in obtaining employment while they are attending KU, so they can earn money for college, develop new job skills, build a resume and gain valuable professional experience. Off-Campus Student Jobs The job location and development (JLD) program sponsored by the University Career Center (UCC) and the Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships locates and develops off-campus job opportunities (full or part-time, seasonal, or temporary) in Lawrence, Topeka and the Kansas City Metropolitan area. All off campus student jobs are posted in Handshake . Featured Resources Handshake Student Employee of the Year SEOTY Winners Federal Work Study Off-Campus Jobs On-Campus Jobs YES Tutor Program Work Study Additional Campus Opportunities All student jobs at the University of Kansas are posted on KU Employment . Other campus positions can be found at: KU Endowment Kansas Union (KU Bookstore, KU Dining and more) KU Medical Center NOTICE: Federal Work Study is managed by the Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships , financialaid@ku.edu / 785-864-4700 . 206 Summerfield Hall 1300 Sunnyside Avenue Lawrence, KS 66045 Bus Routes: 27, 41, 42 ucc@ku.edu 785-864-3624 facebook instagram youtube linkedin People Career Advising Contact Events Visit KU KU Admissions KU Endowment KU News KU Events KU Careers KU Alumni Nondiscrimination statement Accessibility | Website support | CMS login © 2026 The University of Kansas The University of Kansas prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, status as a veteran, sexual orientation, marital status, parental status, gender identity, gender expression, and genetic information in the university's programs and activities. Retaliation is also prohibited by university policy. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the nondiscrimination policies and procedures and is the Title IX Coordinator for all KU and KUMC campuses: Associate Vice Chancellor for the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX, civilrights@ku.edu , Room 1082, Dole Human Development Center, 1000 Sunnyside Avenue, Lawrence, KS 66045, 785-864-6414 , 711 TTY. Reports can be submitted by contacting the Title IX Coordinator as provided herein or using the Title IX online report form and complaints can be submitted with the Title IX Coordinator or using the Title IX online complaint form . The University of Kansas is a public institution governed by the Kansas Board of Regents."
    },
    "https://employment.ku.edu": {
      "title": "Careers",
